('Which question concerns reception history rather than the course’s primary early-context focus?','How later paintings portray Peter’s death',['What social problem an early letter addresses','What an ancient audience might understand by a term','What genre a first-century narrative uses'],'Reception history asks how later communities use and interpret earlier texts.'),
('What does Martin’s emphasis on early Christianities invite students to investigate?','Differences in belief, practice, identity, and social relationships',['A movement with no meaningful disagreements','Only the eventual majority position','A single unchanged institution from the beginning'],'The plural framing directs attention to historical diversity and the processes that later sought unity.'),
